english_question:
Triangle ABC is similar to triangle DEF. Determine the scale factor between the two triangles.
Choices:
(A) \frac { 1 } { 2 }
(B) \frac { 1 } { 1 }
(C) \frac { 2 } { 1 }
(D) \frac { 4 } { 1 }

The figure shows the net of a cube. In this cube, 
① BM is parallel to ED; 
② CN and BE are skew lines; 
③ CN makes a 60° angle with BM; 
④ DM is perpendicular to BN.
Among the four statements above, the correct statement numbers are ( ) 
A. ①②③
B. ②④
C. ③④
D. ②③④

The rectangle ABCD has side lengths AB=4 and AD=2. The rectangle is folded along EF so that point A coincides with point C. After folding, one side is shaded (as shown in the figure). What is the area of the shaded part?
A. 8
B. \frac{11}{2}
C. 4
D. \frac{5}{2}

The three views of a certain geometric body are shown below. What is the surface area of the geometric body? ( )
A. 28+6 \sqrt{5}
B. 30+6 \sqrt{5}
C. 56+12 \sqrt{5}
D. 60+12 \sqrt{5}

The figure shows the three views of a geometric body. The front view is an isosceles right triangle with the hypotenuse BD measuring 2; the side view is a right triangle; the top view is a right trapezoid with AB = BC = 1. What is the volume of this geometric body ( )?
A. \textstyle{\frac{1}{2}}
B. \sqrt{2}
C. \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
D. 1

Which of the four triangles in the square grid below is similar to the triangle in Figure A? ( )
Option A: Triangle with sides 2, \sqrt{10}, 3\sqrt{2}
Option B: Triangle with sides 2, 4, 2\sqrt{5}
Option C: Triangle with sides 2, 3, \sqrt{13}
Option D: Triangle with sides \sqrt{5}, \sqrt{13}, 34
Option E: None
